.TH LCHOWN 3crunch "" "Crunch" "Crunch Library Manual"
.SH NAME
lchown \- change ownership without following a symbolic link
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <unistd.h>
.B int lchown(const char* path, uid_t owner, gid_t group);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Changes ownership of path without following the final symbolic link.
Either ID may be \-1, converted to its respective unsigned type, to leave
that ID unchanged.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns zero, or \-1 with errno set.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR chown (3crunch),
.BR lchown (2)
